    "q-47220": {
      "dom_id": "step-q47220",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "By expressing $\\frac{5}{2}{log}_{2}⁡t$ in the form ${log}_{2}⁡({t}^{k}),$ determine the value of $k.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the power rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡({c}^{m})=m{log}_{n}⁡(c)\n$$\n\nUsing the power rule for logarithms, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}{log}_{2}⁡t & ={log}_{2}⁡({t}^{5/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence $k=\\frac{5}{2}.$",
